# Use-case 02 gap 5 (claim C1): close() around a pack whose template
# holds a `_` hole makes a later overlay statement fill the TEMPLATE
# HOLE instead of merging with the generated child: every child grows
# a bogus `prod:` map, prod.x stays 1, exit 0.  Docs say a generator
# template's `_` is "the source child the generated one is being made
# from" (reference-language.md, "The placeholder `_`"), and the same
# document without close(), or with a hole-free template
# (reference-language.md's own close(pack($.names,{...})) example),
# merges the overlay correctly.
# expected: {"d":...,"deploy":{"dev":{"x":1},"prod":{"x":2}}} exit 0
# actual:   {"d":...,"deploy":{"dev":{"prod":{"x":2},"x":1},
#            "prod":{"prod":{"x":2},"x":1}}} exit 0 (silent corruption)
d: { dev: {}, prod: {} }
deploy: close(pack($.d, _ & { x: ***1 | integer }))
deploy: prod: x: 2
